// What `aibus run` plays back against the fake when no --script is given: look at the top of
// the tree, then answer. A turn ends at its `Stop`, and the next call to the model starts after
// it, so the tail is for the calls that follow in a bigger run (`aibus run --workflow`, which
// the MCP server starts): each later step of a chain, the lead's report on it, and the learning
// extraction at the end, which wants a JSON array and gets an empty one.
[
    Text("I'll start with the top level of the repo."),
    ToolCall(name: "ls", input: {"path": "."}),
    Usage(input: 140, output: 22),
    Stop(ToolUse),
    Text("The repo is a Rust workspace: crates/ holds the engine, the providers and the binary."),
    Usage(input: 260, output: 24),
    Stop(EndTurn),
    Text("Done."),
    Usage(input: 300, output: 2),
    Stop(EndTurn),
    Text("Done."),
    Usage(input: 320, output: 2),
    Stop(EndTurn),
    Text("[]"),
    Usage(input: 340, output: 2),
    Stop(EndTurn),
    Text("[]"),
    Usage(input: 360, output: 2),
    Stop(EndTurn),
]
